WEBVTT

00:00:06.137 --> 00:00:11.647
I share my unstoppable curiosity with you.

00:00:13.727 --> 00:00:17.447
I'm still able to run through the fog...

00:00:17.547 --> 00:00:21.137
...because I know that you're here for me.

00:00:21.237 --> 00:00:28.867
I guess the shape of happiness is different for everyone...

00:00:28.867 --> 00:00:33.207
...however, I know it's boring when I'm alone...

00:00:33.627 --> 00:00:35.087
But, with you...

00:00:35.087 --> 00:00:37.167
...it's like a mystery!

00:00:39.007 --> 00:00:42.757
It's an enchanting future, where...

00:00:42.927 --> 00:00:47.477
...in order for me to be strong, it's always you...

00:00:47.477 --> 00:00:51.857
...that I can continue to depend on, right?

00:00:51.857 --> 00:00:53.437
Just to survive!

00:00:53.607 --> 00:00:55.397
Stumped Q? Don't lose your way!

00:00:55.397 --> 00:00:57.237
Take this moment...

00:00:57.237 --> 00:01:00.857
...to fix your gaze and charge on ahead!

00:01:00.857 --> 00:01:03.067
Eternally, we'll always be together...

00:01:03.067 --> 00:01:04.907
...searching and pursuing...

00:01:04.907 --> 00:01:08.617
...the meaning of it all.

00:01:08.617 --> 00:01:10.747
Truth is nothing but a labyrinth...

00:01:10.747 --> 00:01:12.457
...that we try to continue through...

00:01:12.457 --> 00:01:16.127
...especially when we are hurt.

00:01:16.127 --> 00:01:18.297
I'll take you, so come this way.

00:01:18.297 --> 00:01:20.127
I'm certain that, on that day...

00:01:20.127 --> 00:01:24.047
...I'll see your smile, face to face!

00:01:46.647 --> 00:01:48.182
You must be tired.

00:01:48.249 --> 00:01:49.917
Thank you for picking me up.

00:01:50.751 --> 00:01:52.853
Should we proceed to the estate for today?

00:01:52.853 --> 00:01:53.221
No.

00:01:54.956 --> 00:01:56.324
Proceed to DDS.

00:01:57.892 --> 00:01:58.993
Right away?

00:01:59.827 --> 00:02:00.394
Yeah.

00:02:01.128 --> 00:02:02.230
Right away…

00:02:05.733 --> 00:02:08.269
Hey! How do you know about that?

00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:12.974
W-well, I was sort of practicing trailing someone…

00:02:13.207 --> 00:02:13.941
And…

00:02:15.643 --> 00:02:20.081
You suddenly started to run, so I kept
a close eye so as not to lose you.

00:02:21.716 --> 00:02:23.217
And then, I saw them by accident.

00:02:24.118 --> 00:02:27.855
It’s because you tripped so spectacularly
in the middle of the road.

00:02:28.456 --> 00:02:29.090
You pervert!

00:02:29.590 --> 00:02:31.392
N-No, you see, it wasn’t intentional.

00:02:31.592 --> 00:02:34.028
You were following me without my permission!

00:02:32.875 --> 00:02:34.025
They’re so immature.

00:02:34.195 --> 00:02:34.996
It’s inexcusable!

00:02:35.363 --> 00:02:39.300
N-No, you see, we haven’t practiced
tracking people yet, so…

00:02:36.775 --> 00:02:39.075
Is that something a grade schooler should say?

00:02:39.333 --> 00:02:41.936
I'm talking about mental age!

00:02:42.703 --> 00:02:44.205
And besides, it wasn’t just me!

00:02:44.739 --> 00:02:47.575
Kinta saw Megu’s polka-dotted panties too!

00:02:52.146 --> 00:02:53.147
Hey everyone!

00:02:53.981 --> 00:02:55.483
You perverts!

00:02:55.483 --> 00:02:56.484
Headmaster Dan!

00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:05.192
What are you guys doing?

00:03:05.726 --> 00:03:07.428
You almost injured Headmaster Dan!

00:03:08.329 --> 00:03:09.630
We’re sorry.

00:03:10.898 --> 00:03:13.067
If I remain with these guys…

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:29.784
That must be nice for Saburoumaru-san, getting
to practice in a real investigation.

00:03:29.984 --> 00:03:31.218
On the first day of school too.

00:03:31.218 --> 00:03:32.620
I guess that’s the kind of class Class A is.

00:03:32.787 --> 00:03:35.690
What are you fussing about?
Hurry and take your seats!

00:03:35.956 --> 00:03:36.824
Yes!

00:03:38.392 --> 00:03:40.161
I have a favor to ask you, Dan-sensei.

00:03:41.462 --> 00:03:42.363
What is it?

00:03:43.097 --> 00:03:47.568
Can I join Class A’s practice
investigation session too?

00:03:48.769 --> 00:03:50.004
Why do you want to do that?

00:03:51.105 --> 00:03:53.974
It’s possible to change classes if
my grades are good enough?

00:03:55.609 --> 00:03:59.046
Fine. I'll permit Class Q to join the session.

00:03:59.613 --> 00:04:00.481
Really!?

00:04:01.315 --> 00:04:01.615
What?

00:04:03.718 --> 00:04:04.852
Yeah!

00:04:05.019 --> 00:04:06.754
Yeah! Yeah!

00:04:08.322 --> 00:04:11.258
I wanted to join the session by myself…

00:04:12.259 --> 00:04:15.196
You guys are in charge of the
investigation from now on.

00:04:16.163 --> 00:04:18.833
I will be giving you a minimum of advice.

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:25.172
All of you will take the initiative and solve this case
as DDS’s representatives in this investigation.

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:27.675
They have a tight security system.

00:04:27.908 --> 00:04:30.745
Which means that an outsider couldn’t
have committed the crime,

00:04:31.545 --> 00:04:33.180
Let’s go, Saburoumaru!

00:04:34.448 --> 00:04:35.149
Y-yes!

00:04:35.583 --> 00:04:38.085
Remember, Class Q is just here to watch.

00:04:38.352 --> 00:04:39.420
Don’t get in our way.

00:04:46.794 --> 00:04:48.062
I'm Octori Shizuko.

00:04:48.596 --> 00:04:51.232
Thank you for coming to investigate.

00:04:52.032 --> 00:04:52.933
This way please.

00:04:53.501 --> 00:04:56.170
Nothing has been touched during the
week since the incident took place.

00:04:59.507 --> 00:05:02.777
The victim was my father, Ootori Mitsugu.

00:05:03.511 --> 00:05:05.813
He was a sports commentator
specializing in F-1 races.

00:05:07.148 --> 00:05:09.784
The police ruled this case an accidental death…

00:05:10.117 --> 00:05:12.219
But I'm not convinced.

00:05:13.354 --> 00:05:15.623
I want to know what really happened to my father.

00:05:17.224 --> 00:05:17.992
This is?

00:05:18.559 --> 00:05:24.131
The police have already collected the pieces,
but a flowerpot shattered there.

00:05:29.837 --> 00:05:36.343
According to the report, the flowerpot fell from
the balcony above and struck him on the head.

00:05:36.710 --> 00:05:39.513
And that proved to be fatal.

00:05:40.381 --> 00:05:44.018
The cause of death was cerebral hemorrhaging.
There were no other external wounds.

00:05:47.321 --> 00:05:49.990
Who lives above here?

00:05:50.758 --> 00:05:53.127
It’s my father’s assistant, Honda-san’s room.

00:05:53.694 --> 00:05:55.930
Then, the flowerpot was Honda-san’s?

00:05:56.630 --> 00:05:58.899
I said Class Q is just here to watch.

00:06:03.003 --> 00:06:05.506
Father was found lying here in a heap.

00:06:06.574 --> 00:06:08.876
It was as if he had fallen forward on the desk.

00:06:14.348 --> 00:06:17.151
It looks like he was working on some
type of report, doesn’t it?

00:06:17.585 --> 00:06:17.885
Huh?

00:06:19.086 --> 00:06:20.321
What does that say?

00:06:22.389 --> 00:06:25.259
Rijhntunbm5yegfb?

00:06:25.259 --> 00:06:26.827
Is it some kind of good luck charm?

00:06:27.495 --> 00:06:28.462
You’re all wrong.

00:06:29.396 --> 00:06:30.664
It’s a code.

00:06:31.131 --> 00:06:34.034
Moreover, it’s the victim’s dying message.

00:06:40.307 --> 00:06:41.475
Dying message?

00:06:41.909 --> 00:06:43.277
It’s not ’dim’ng’ you know.

00:06:43.377 --> 00:06:45.045
And of course, it’s not ’diving’ either.

00:06:45.045 --> 00:06:46.247
I know that!

00:06:47.448 --> 00:06:49.850
Can Class Q decipher it, I wonder.

00:06:49.850 --> 00:06:50.417
Umm…

00:06:50.985 --> 00:06:52.086
Maybe that’s it!

00:06:52.319 --> 00:06:52.553
Eh?

00:06:52.553 --> 00:06:53.020
What?

00:06:53.721 --> 00:06:57.892
Look! The keyboard has both
English and kana inputs.

00:06:58.125 --> 00:07:00.628
So if we match up the corresponding keys…

00:07:00.928 --> 00:07:08.836
su ku ma ku mika na ko mo mi e n i ki ha ko…?

00:07:09.069 --> 00:07:10.471
What does that mean?

00:07:10.838 --> 00:07:11.472
Dunno.

00:07:12.406 --> 00:07:14.141
So do you think you can decipher it?

00:07:14.842 --> 00:07:16.844
I-I was going to start that now…

00:07:18.145 --> 00:07:19.813
I'll do the deciphering.

00:07:20.614 --> 00:07:23.551
Any kind of encrypted code must follow a fixed rule.

00:07:24.485 --> 00:07:27.788
For example, the letter-swapping rule where you
replace each letter with a different letter.

00:07:27.922 --> 00:07:30.190
Or the location-changing rule where
you change the order of the letters.

00:07:30.491 --> 00:07:33.594
Or the letter-insertion rule where you insert
a specific letter into parts of the sentence.

00:07:33.861 --> 00:07:37.264
There are many other types of
rules associated with codes.

00:07:37.531 --> 00:07:40.434
And this program tests all those rules
and checks if any of them applies.

00:07:41.702 --> 00:07:43.771
Deciphering software, eh?

00:07:43.837 --> 00:07:44.772
Where did you get that from?

00:07:44.905 --> 00:07:46.073
I created it myself.

00:07:47.207 --> 00:07:51.245
You aren’t called the genius boy
programmer for nothing!

00:07:51.679 --> 00:07:52.846
Is that so?

00:07:53.147 --> 00:07:55.716
You might be more suited for Class A.

00:07:56.717 --> 00:07:59.420
I can put in a good word for you if you want.

00:07:59.453 --> 00:08:01.555
Really? Please do so.

00:08:01.622 --> 00:08:03.557
Well, it all depends on how well you decipher this.

00:08:03.857 --> 00:08:04.558
Alright!

00:08:07.728 --> 00:08:08.762
Wow…

00:08:08.829 --> 00:08:10.264
Can you really decipher it with this thing?

00:08:10.564 --> 00:08:11.699
Do you think it can?

00:08:12.066 --> 00:08:13.033
I doubt it.

00:08:13.400 --> 00:08:14.168
Who knows.

00:08:14.435 --> 00:08:15.703
But, you know…

00:08:15.703 --> 00:08:16.804
Please don’t disturb me!

00:08:17.204 --> 00:08:18.505
We’re not trying to disturb you!

00:08:18.505 --> 00:08:19.473
Well you are disturbing me!

00:08:19.907 --> 00:08:25.512
I'm planning on solving this case so that Dan-sensei
will recognize my talent and promote me to Class A!

00:08:25.779 --> 00:08:29.984
That’s why all of us should work hard
together and aim for the upper class!

00:08:30.284 --> 00:08:30.818
Yeah, yeah!

00:08:31.218 --> 00:08:32.786
I didn’t say I was going with the rest of you!

00:08:34.388 --> 00:08:35.422
I'm going by myself.

00:08:36.023 --> 00:08:37.691
You guys can just remain in the same class…

00:08:37.891 --> 00:08:39.493
Hey! What do you mean?

00:08:39.627 --> 00:08:40.995
Isn’t it obvious!

00:08:41.362 --> 00:08:45.633
He’s saying that nothing good will happen
if he bangs around with you guys.

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:46.700
Right?

00:08:46.967 --> 00:08:47.434
Yes!

00:08:47.568 --> 00:08:51.038
Now, hurry and finish it. Don’t
waste time talking to them.

00:08:51.105 --> 00:08:52.106
Mamma-kun…

00:08:54.775 --> 00:08:56.677
If that’s what you want then go ahead!

00:08:57.011 --> 00:09:00.414
Let’s go, Kyuu, Megu. Let’s
go investigate other stuff.

00:09:02.282 --> 00:09:05.319
Excuse me, can we ask some questions
to the other residents of the house?

00:09:05.586 --> 00:09:06.453
Please come this way.

00:09:13.661 --> 00:09:16.497
I was away from the house at the time.

00:09:16.530 --> 00:09:19.900
But according to the testimonies, there
were three other people here then.

00:09:21.101 --> 00:09:22.870
The first one was Honda Keiko-san.

00:09:23.237 --> 00:09:26.240
She's well versed in various languages and served as my father's assistant.

00:09:23.237 --> 00:09:31.145
She accompanied him as his translator whenever he
went abroad to collect information for his reports.

00:09:31.979 --> 00:09:36.216
But it seems that they’ve had an argument
concerning her wages recently.

00:09:36.650 --> 00:09:38.919
I was about to quit this job anyway.

00:09:42.589 --> 00:09:47.194
I've been wanting to move on, but l can’t leave
until I resolve the issue of that book.

00:09:47.594 --> 00:09:48.796
What do you mean by "that book"?

00:09:49.830 --> 00:09:53.333
An interview collection of F-1 racers
that he published last year.

00:09:54.168 --> 00:09:56.003
Even though he was only able
to complete that book…

00:09:56.003 --> 00:09:59.773
…because of the personal connections
that I established…

00:10:00.841 --> 00:10:03.010
He said he wouldn’t give me any royalties
from that book whatsoever!

00:10:05.112 --> 00:10:06.980
Where was the flowerpot kept?

00:10:08.282 --> 00:10:09.349
Somewhere over there.

00:10:14.955 --> 00:10:15.689
Right here?

00:10:16.223 --> 00:10:16.790
Yeah.

00:10:17.024 --> 00:10:17.524
Megu!

00:10:19.226 --> 00:10:19.827
Right.

00:10:20.327 --> 00:10:23.997
Then, somebody moved the flowerpot?

00:10:24.932 --> 00:10:26.800
l guess that must be true.

00:10:30.671 --> 00:10:32.506
The second person is Kawase-san.

00:10:33.173 --> 00:10:37.611
He’s been serving my father as his manager
since he retired from F-3 racing.

00:10:38.479 --> 00:10:40.814
But my father was quite a bossy guy.

00:10:40.948 --> 00:10:44.051
So whenever something bothered him, he
often vented his anger on Kawase-san.

00:10:44.818 --> 00:10:47.354
It seems that he took it out on
Kawase-san again recently.

00:10:47.654 --> 00:10:48.388
Excuse me!

00:10:49.456 --> 00:10:51.558
Can we ask some questions?

00:10:52.059 --> 00:10:52.793
Sure.

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:57.264
Is it true ihat you were the first
one to find Ootori-san’s body?

00:10:57.531 --> 00:11:01.869
Yes. He had a meeting scheduled for that
afternoon so I came to pick him up.

00:11:02.336 --> 00:11:03.904
Sensei! Sensei!

00:11:04.571 --> 00:11:05.305
What’s wrong?

00:11:06.039 --> 00:11:06.907
The door is locked.

00:11:10.711 --> 00:11:11.345
Sensei…

00:11:18.619 --> 00:11:20.954
I didn’t expect to see him like that.

00:11:21.822 --> 00:11:22.689
Uhm…

00:11:22.689 --> 00:11:23.891
One more thing.

00:11:24.691 --> 00:11:28.662
Do you know where the flowerpot
was originally located?

00:11:29.429 --> 00:11:33.300
No. I've never been inside her room.

00:11:34.434 --> 00:11:35.502
Thank you for your time.

00:11:36.770 --> 00:11:39.940
The last one is my stepmother, Mayumi-san.

00:11:40.641 --> 00:11:43.343
She married my father when I was 10…

00:11:43.410 --> 00:11:46.680
…and since then, we’ve been living
together happily in this house.

00:11:47.314 --> 00:11:50.584
Although it seems she was having some
trouble with my father recently.

00:11:50.884 --> 00:11:52.419
But she wouldn’t do something like that.

00:11:54.988 --> 00:11:58.826
Yes. It was all just as Kawase-kun told you.

00:11:59.793 --> 00:12:00.561
At that time…

00:12:00.761 --> 00:12:02.062
Sensei! Sensei!

00:12:03.564 --> 00:12:04.298
Madame…

00:12:05.866 --> 00:12:07.100
Call the ambulance! Quickly!

00:12:07.668 --> 00:12:08.202
Yes!

00:12:10.370 --> 00:12:11.104
Dear…

00:12:14.141 --> 00:12:18.846
Although he was that kind of guy, it was
still heartbreaking to see him dead.

00:12:18.846 --> 00:12:20.714
Mother, that’s enough for now.

00:12:22.382 --> 00:12:22.716
Uhm…

00:12:22.716 --> 00:12:24.251
One more thing.

00:12:24.918 --> 00:12:27.688
Have you ever moved Honda-san’s
flowerpot before?

00:12:28.822 --> 00:12:29.823
I couldn’t possibly.

00:12:29.923 --> 00:12:33.660
Although I'm the landlord, I'd never go into
a tenant’s room without their permission.

00:12:34.361 --> 00:12:35.796
Thank you for your time.

00:12:38.765 --> 00:12:41.802
That flowerpot couldn’t have moved by itself…

00:12:42.903 --> 00:12:45.272
One of those three people is lying to us.

00:12:45.672 --> 00:12:48.642
But why did the police rule this case an accident?

00:12:48.842 --> 00:12:50.510
Probably because there wasn’t any evidence.

00:12:50.844 --> 00:12:52.045
If that’s the case…

00:12:52.246 --> 00:12:53.847
We only have that message after all.

00:12:54.748 --> 00:12:56.116
Hey, Kyuu!

00:12:58.685 --> 00:13:00.487
Why? Damn it!

00:13:04.291 --> 00:13:07.227
Perhaps I was wrong to rely on you.

00:13:09.062 --> 00:13:10.998
There’s no code that I can’t decipher!

00:13:11.131 --> 00:13:14.801
Let’s see, if it’s the method of changing
the letters to zodiacal signs…

00:13:14.868 --> 00:13:17.437
…used in Oguri Mushitaro’s National
History Museum murder case…

00:13:17.437 --> 00:13:20.674
R will be Cancer, I will be Leo, and J…

00:13:20.908 --> 00:13:21.842
There’s no!.

00:13:23.944 --> 00:13:25.112
How's it going, Kazuma-kun?

00:13:25.379 --> 00:13:26.713
Damn it! How about this!

00:13:28.982 --> 00:13:29.816
This is no good, either!

00:13:33.654 --> 00:13:35.822
Was it really a dying message?

00:13:37.591 --> 00:13:41.828
lt could’ve happened when Kawase-san shock
Octori-san’s body to check on him…

00:13:42.462 --> 00:13:45.499
Sensei! Sensei! Sensei!

00:13:46.099 --> 00:13:49.202
Perhaps Ootori-san’s hand got dragged
along and hit the keys.

00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:51.471
Maybe that’s what happened!

00:13:52.673 --> 00:13:55.075
You’re just saying that because
you can’t solve it by yourself!

00:13:59.212 --> 00:14:01.982
I-I’s all your fault for saying such strange things.

00:14:02.482 --> 00:14:03.283
Why you!

00:14:04.184 --> 00:14:06.486
I think it’s a dying message.

00:14:07.921 --> 00:14:11.625
If it was really an accident, instead
of going to the computer…

00:14:11.725 --> 00:14:14.528
…I think he would have gone to the phone
or to the door to call for help.

00:14:15.162 --> 00:14:17.698
He went to the computer to leave something.

00:14:18.999 --> 00:14:23.470
He probably saw somebody’s face when
the flowerpot came falling down.

00:14:27.541 --> 00:14:29.910
So, Kazuma-kun! Do your best to decipher it!

00:14:32.112 --> 00:14:33.747
I would do it even if you didn’t ask me.

00:14:34.348 --> 00:14:37.150
Oh, then, I'll go take a run around neighborhood.

00:14:37.351 --> 00:14:37.718
Eh?

00:14:38.085 --> 00:14:38.552
Huh?

00:14:39.521 --> 00:14:40.856
I'm going to think a little more.

00:14:41.690 --> 00:14:46.294
But I get tired using just my head so
I sometimes go move my body a bit.

00:14:47.662 --> 00:14:48.663
H-hey!

00:14:57.839 --> 00:14:58.507
Come in.

00:15:02.744 --> 00:15:05.547
I brought you some evening snacks,
young master Kazuma.

00:15:06.781 --> 00:15:07.249
Thanks.

00:15:15.924 --> 00:15:19.895
It’s young master’s favorite, a Homard Sandwich.

00:15:22.330 --> 00:15:24.566
If you need something else, please call me.

00:15:24.633 --> 00:15:25.066
Okay.

00:15:27.168 --> 00:15:28.303
Damn it!

00:15:34.175 --> 00:15:37.479
It’s no use! The code doesn’t turn
into any meaningful words.

00:15:38.480 --> 00:15:41.283
Maybe it’s not a code after all?

00:15:42.050 --> 00:15:46.054
I get tired using just my head so I sometimes
go move my body a bit.

00:15:51.960 --> 00:15:53.562
I guess he didn’t mean it that way.

00:16:00.936 --> 00:16:03.405
I wonder if Kazuma-kun has deciphered it yet.

00:16:06.274 --> 00:16:08.610
It’s no use! I can’t decipher it.

00:16:10.045 --> 00:16:11.179
I quit.

00:16:22.691 --> 00:16:25.694
Could this be?

00:16:37.939 --> 00:16:40.041
I see! I've got it!

00:16:43.345 --> 00:16:46.548
That’s it! Alright! I've done it!

00:16:46.715 --> 00:16:47.282
Oh, yeah!

00:16:52.587 --> 00:16:53.088
Yes.

00:16:54.823 --> 00:16:55.890
Narusawa-san?

00:16:56.257 --> 00:16:58.693
Oh, his friend from the detective academy.

00:16:58.994 --> 00:17:01.363
Nice to meet you, I'm Kyuu’s mother.

00:17:02.364 --> 00:17:03.765
Yes. Good evening to you too.

00:17:04.065 --> 00:17:07.636
Kyuu’s in the bath now. Shall
I tell him to call you back?

00:17:08.003 --> 00:17:11.973
No. That’s okay. Sorry for
calling you so late at night.

00:17:13.942 --> 00:17:18.480
There was no need to call Kyuu-san.
What was I thinking?

00:17:20.382 --> 00:17:22.617
I'm the only one who will be promoted to Class A!

00:17:26.955 --> 00:17:28.089
Mom, I'm done.

00:17:28.423 --> 00:17:30.725
Oh, good. Your friend just called for you.

00:17:31.292 --> 00:17:32.060
Kazuma-kun?

00:17:32.494 --> 00:17:37.065
Yeah. But asked him if you should call
him back and he said it was okay.

00:17:38.333 --> 00:17:41.302
He seems like a real mature boy. He’s
only a grade schooler though, right?

00:17:49.144 --> 00:17:51.212
Could it be that Kazuma-kun…

00:17:54.916 --> 00:17:55.483
Kyuu!

00:17:56.351 --> 00:17:57.152
Kinta! Megu!

00:17:58.153 --> 00:18:00.088
He deciphered the dying message?

00:18:00.388 --> 00:18:01.122
Yeah, most likely…

00:18:01.856 --> 00:18:03.158
But I can’t reach him on the phone.

00:18:03.992 --> 00:18:07.328
I think Ranma-kun might have
gone to Ootori-san’s residence.

00:18:07.495 --> 00:18:08.963
What? Then…

00:18:09.330 --> 00:18:13.301
Yeah. A little kid like him going straight
to the culprit is dangerous!

00:18:13.668 --> 00:18:14.035
Let’s go!

00:18:14.202 --> 00:18:14.636
Yeah!

00:18:18.940 --> 00:18:20.275
Good evening.

00:18:21.009 --> 00:18:21.943
Shizuko-san?

00:18:28.349 --> 00:18:29.184
Excuse me!

00:18:30.051 --> 00:18:31.453
You startled me!

00:18:31.920 --> 00:18:34.656
You’re the detective from earlier, right?

00:18:34.956 --> 00:18:36.624
What are you doing this late at night…?

00:18:37.158 --> 00:18:39.728
The one who murdered Ootori Mitsugu-san is…

00:18:40.095 --> 00:18:42.163
..you, Ootori Mayumi-san!

00:18:43.531 --> 00:18:46.835
Oh, my. What are you saying so abruptly?

00:18:48.503 --> 00:18:49.971
Do you have any evidence?

00:18:50.605 --> 00:18:52.807
The evidence is this!

00:18:56.077 --> 00:18:57.245
What part of that is the evidence?

00:18:57.812 --> 00:19:00.548
I couldn’t get it when I was using just my head.

00:19:01.149 --> 00:19:05.687
But the mystery unraveled as I moved
my fingers while typing.

00:19:07.922 --> 00:19:10.525
R, l,J , H, N make Ma.

00:19:11.259 --> 00:19:14.095
T, U, N, B, M make Yu.

00:19:14.662 --> 00:19:17.665
5, V, E, G, F, B make Mi.

00:19:24.272 --> 00:19:27.275
When the flowerpot fell on Ootori-san…

00:19:28.576 --> 00:19:29.344
Mayumi?

00:19:30.712 --> 00:19:31.579
He saw you!

00:19:35.650 --> 00:19:39.921
That’s why he wrote your name with the keyboard!

00:19:41.256 --> 00:19:42.223
Am I wrong?

00:19:43.158 --> 00:19:45.827
Oh, so that’s what that meant.

00:19:46.528 --> 00:19:46.928
And?

00:19:48.062 --> 00:19:49.063
W-what do you mean "And"?

00:19:49.664 --> 00:19:50.799
Do you have any evidence?

00:19:51.032 --> 00:19:52.534
This is the evidence!

00:19:53.968 --> 00:19:58.606
You’re really a kid after all. Something like
that is only circumstantial evidence.

00:19:59.407 --> 00:20:01.709
Hey! How long do you intend to hide like that?

00:20:02.043 --> 00:20:03.511
Come out already.

00:20:03.511 --> 00:20:03.945
Eh?

00:20:09.617 --> 00:20:13.121
If you were a normal kid, we wouldn’t
mind letting you go, but…

00:20:13.421 --> 00:20:15.156
You’re an agent from DDS.

00:20:15.657 --> 00:20:19.427
D-Don’t come near me! If you do, I'll call the police…

00:20:20.228 --> 00:20:20.929
M-My cellphone…

00:20:24.532 --> 00:20:24.933
Hey!

00:20:26.034 --> 00:20:27.402
What are you doing? Hurry up!

00:20:33.641 --> 00:20:34.642
Help me!

00:20:35.643 --> 00:20:37.345
Hey, the people upstairs will hear!

00:20:37.912 --> 00:20:38.813
That’s true…

00:20:39.247 --> 00:20:42.517
I'm sorry, but we can’t go back now…

00:20:50.658 --> 00:20:51.759
Please stop, Mother!

00:20:52.260 --> 00:20:52.927
Shizuko-san!

00:20:53.895 --> 00:20:54.462
Kazuma!

00:20:55.363 --> 00:20:56.931
Kyuu! Kinta! Megu!

00:21:04.239 --> 00:21:04.806
Kazuma!

00:21:05.039 --> 00:21:05.640
Kyuu…

00:21:06.341 --> 00:21:07.041
Megu…

00:21:07.041 --> 00:21:07.775
Are you alright?

00:21:08.376 --> 00:21:10.278
We made it in time because you called me.

00:21:11.646 --> 00:21:12.113
Y-Yeah…

00:21:21.489 --> 00:21:22.023
Mother.

00:21:22.824 --> 00:21:26.327
Why? You got along so well up until now.

00:21:29.097 --> 00:21:34.269
You might not believe me, but I never thought
of doing it until that moment.

00:21:34.969 --> 00:21:38.640
It’s just that, when! looked down, he was there…

00:21:41.042 --> 00:21:47.548
As I looked at him, the stress that had built-up
over the years turned into spite…

00:21:55.156 --> 00:21:56.257
I'm sorry.

00:22:12.373 --> 00:22:16.244
Everybody has various circumstances
that they live with…

00:22:17.111 --> 00:22:20.648
And it is often the case that they try
to escape those circumstances.

00:22:21.149 --> 00:22:27.021
Pursuing a case may result in a sad
conclusion for the people involved.

00:22:27.588 --> 00:22:31.526
And you also have to be ready to risk
your own life to solve the case.

00:22:33.227 --> 00:22:36.998
We all have accepted that fact.

00:22:37.799 --> 00:22:40.768
Yes. I'm sorry. I'll think that over…

00:22:42.236 --> 00:22:44.472
Anyway, I'm surprised you were able to solve it.

00:22:45.139 --> 00:22:47.041
Yes! It’s all thanks to Kyuu!

00:22:47.909 --> 00:22:48.743
What do you mean?

00:22:49.344 --> 00:22:54.582
You gave me a hint to move my body
instead of just using my head.

00:22:55.283 --> 00:22:57.151
A hint? What do you mean?

00:22:58.353 --> 00:23:02.357
I got it when! moved my finger while
typing that word so many times.

00:23:02.623 --> 00:23:07.328
Wow! You’re awesome, Kazuma! You
solved the case with just that?

00:23:07.495 --> 00:23:09.397
Well, I guess you could say that.

00:23:09.897 --> 00:23:11.399
Geez! You really get carried away easy.

00:23:13.368 --> 00:23:14.202
By the way, Kazuma!

00:23:14.736 --> 00:23:18.406
If you want to move your body, let’s go
to the martial arts gym after class!

00:23:18.506 --> 00:23:21.309
N-no. I'm fine!

00:23:21.776 --> 00:23:24.912
A sound mind in a sound body!

00:23:25.446 --> 00:23:25.947
Here!

00:23:26.981 --> 00:23:30.685
Please stop! I hate sweaty stuff!

00:23:31.419 --> 00:23:32.854
Please let me go!

00:23:36.681 --> 00:23:47.611
Unable to cry in front of you, I'm whistling instead.

00:23:50.321 --> 00:24:02.171
Saying "I'll always be beside you" without saying a single word.

00:24:02.171 --> 00:24:09.261
My loving heart is overflowing; those sad thoughts...

00:24:09.261 --> 00:24:14.891
are like things that fade away unnoticed in mid-air.

00:24:15.091 --> 00:24:21.101
And again, with a mighty smile of relief...

00:24:21.231 --> 00:24:26.651
I will see you off.

00:24:26.901 --> 00:24:36.491
Goodbye and thank you.

00:24:39.352 --> 00:24:41.187
A suspect who has 1000 witnesses.

00:24:41.888 --> 00:24:44.924
We’re at a loss facing this unbreakable alibi.

00:24:45.558 --> 00:24:46.660
A maid being ran down.

00:24:47.093 --> 00:24:48.461
A surging murderous intent.

00:24:49.129 --> 00:24:52.432
Can Kinta’s investigation expose the culprit?

00:24:53.533 --> 00:24:54.567
There’s only one answer!

00:25:07.947 --> 00:25:10.617
Huh!? I sense something.
